artup_lock` in both the normal and the `RuntimeError` workaround branch.\n  - New `_startup_sequence()` is the idempotent, lock-guarded entry point. It runs the immutable table-count precompute once, then calls `invoke_startup()`.\n  - `app()` drops the local `setup_db`. It wraps `AsgiLifespan` with `on_startup=[self._startup_sequence]` and `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` with the same hook.\n- **`datasette/utils/asgi.py`**\n  - `AsgiLifespan` catches startup and shutdown exceptions and sends `lifespan.startup.failed` / `lifespan.shutdown.failed` with the message.\n  - `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` gets an `asyncio.Lock`. It passes lifespan scopes straight through, and for other scopes it runs the hooks under the lock and sets `_started` only afterwards.\n- **`datasette/cli.py`**: `serve` calls `ds._startup_sequence()` instead of `ds.invoke_startup()`, with the comment updated.\n\nI didn't edit the test file and didn't run the wider test suite. I also haven't committed anything; the changes are in the working tree alongside the untracked `SPEC.md`.", "ttft_ms": 1622, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 27534, "uuid": "ea27820a-4e92-4099-8ea2-d320ed1f778c", "ttft_stream_ms": 1377, "time_to_request_ms": 242, "first_content_frame_ms": 1377, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
